  "analysis": "Market regime is mixed with a mild portfolio drawdown (-2.49%, no forced de-risking actions). Forecast medians show no directional skill, so I lean on interval width (reliable risk signal) and recent price action. Broad US (A02) is the calmest asset (9.5% vol, narrowest 5d interval 3.46%); bonds (A09) are the second-narrowest interval with positive 1d/5d returns and low vol — both are the right ballast in a drawdown, so I keep the existing overweights. Tech (A11) has 20d momentum (+5.6%) but a 5d pullback, so it stays modestly above baseline. Energy is the one clear momentum pocket (A03 5d +5.4%, 1d +1.8%; A13 5d +5.8%), but both carry very high vol (22-24%) and wide intervals, so I add only the energy ETF A03 at its baseline weight for diversification, funded from cash, and skip the single-stock A13. Emerging (A12), gold (A05), and the high-vol tech/health single stocks (A01, A07, A14) stay at zero: wide intervals, weak or no momentum, and no edge in a drawdown. A10 is skipped as redundant with A02 and negative 20d momentum. Result: keep the defensive core (A02, A09, A04, A06), add A03 at baseline, hold cash at ~20.7% (well above the 10% floor) as a drawdown buffer. All group, asset-type, and increase-cap constraints are satisfied; the only >2pp trades are A03 0→4.83% and cash 25.56%→20.73%.",
